    "narrative": "For the June 22nd slate, the **Austin Waves** offense is anchored by **Jackson Merrill** (74.60) and **Gunnar Henderson** (66.81). **Jackson Merrill** holds the day's highest efficiency rating, benefitting from a premium matchup against Grant Holmes, where a strong platoon advantage (+13%) and a top-of-the-order boost create elite scoring potential. Simultaneously, **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo** (64.44) capitalize on a high-ceiling matchup against the struggling Sam Aldegheri (5.75 xERA). While **Gunnar Henderson** faces a slight penalty for the L/L dynamic, his raw talent and placement in the #2 hole outweigh the platoon friction. **Andy Pages** (62.80) and **Kyle Tucker** (66.62) are also high-leverage starts today, with **Andy Pages** specifically flagged for his potential to exploit the slow delivery of the opposition, increasing his utility in our pursuit of stolen bases.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Miguel Vargas**, who landed at a 47.86 efficiency score. While he remains a capable contributor, the optimizer opted for the higher-floor consistency of **Dominic Smith** and **Josh Jung** to round out the starting nine. **Miguel Vargas** suffered specifically from a negative park factor and an elite hold rating from Gavin Williams, which suppressed his stolen base upside and overall offensive projection compared to our other utility options. We are also closely monitoring the lineup status of **Drake Baldwin**, **Brayan Rocchio**, **Wade Meckler**, **Andy Pages**, **Kyle Tucker**, and **Coby Mayo**; as these positions remain \"Lineup Pending,\" any drastic shifts in batting order\u2014particularly for **Drake Baldwin** and **Wade Meckler**\u2014could necessitate a last-minute adjustment to our daily rotation strategy to preserve our game cap efficiency.",
